- Bilateral knee swelling with sequential onset (left then right), now active unilateral inflammation (right knee: warm, tender, swollen, reduced ROM);  
- No recollection of prior arthritis type or testing;  
- No current medications, allergies, exposures, or systemic symptoms;  
