Despite incomplete data, the clinical picture — acute, warm, tender, swollen monoarticular knee in a patient with prior arthritis — most strongly suggests **gout** or **pseudogout**, with gout being slightly more common in this presentation. However, per protocol, I must issue [FINISH] now — no further turns remain.

